The previous attempt to generate an OWL Turtle fragment for this table failed to parse. Generate a SIMPLER version that is guaranteed to parse.

Use these namespace prefixes (already declared — do not redeclare):
  @prefix ind:  <{ontology_prefix}> .
  @prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
  @prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
  @prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
  @prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
  @prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .

[CONTEXT]
Table name (PascalCase for class):   {table_class_name}
Source table identifier:              {table_name}

Database schema:
{schema_context}

[STRICT OUTPUT CONSTRAINTS]
Produce ONLY these triple patterns, one per line, separated by `.`:

  ind:ClassName a owl:Class .
  ind:ClassName rdfs:label "Human Readable Name" .
  ind:ClassName rdfs:comment "Description text" .
  ind:propertyName a owl:ObjectProperty .
  ind:propertyName a owl:DatatypeProperty .
  ind:propertyName rdfs:label "Property Label" .
  ind:propertyName rdfs:comment "Property description" .
  ind:propertyName rdfs:domain ind:ClassName .
  ind:propertyName rdfs:range xsd:string .
  ind:propertyName rdfs:range ind:OtherClass .
  ind:propertyName prov:wasDerivedFrom <{provenance_base}/{table_name}/COLUMN_NAME> .

Valid xsd datatypes (use ONLY these for rdfs:range on DatatypeProperties):
  xsd:string, xsd:integer, xsd:decimal, xsd:float, xsd:double, xsd:boolean, xsd:dateTime
DO NOT use xsd:date — it is rejected by OWL 2 DL reasoners.

DO NOT emit ANY of the following. If you emit any of these, the parse
WILL fail and the entire table's fragment will be lost:
  - Blank nodes in any position: `[ ... ]`, `[]`, `[a owl:Restriction ...]`
  - owl:Restriction, owl:onProperty, owl:minCardinality, owl:maxCardinality, owl:cardinality
  - Inline property lists: `ind:X rdfs:label "A" ; rdfs:comment "B" .`
  - Comma-separated objects: `rdfs:range xsd:string, xsd:integer`
  - Any `a` shortcut except at start of a type declaration
  - Any nested structures

EVERY line must be a complete flat triple ending with ` .` (period).
One subject, one predicate, one object, one period.

Do not wrap in markdown fences. Do not add explanatory text. Output
only valid Turtle triples, one per line.
